{ Lasker plans. Learn the pawn break: a central push that challenges his pawn and frees your own pieces. Push yours to d5. [%cal Yd7d5] } 3... d5 { Your bishop on c8 finally gets a diagonal. Development comes before pawn hunting. [%cal Gd7d5] } (3... Nc6 { Also playable. Your knight goes to c6. } 4. cxd4 { Playable, but your pawn break on d5 already frees the bishop — no detour needed. [%cal Bc3d4] }) (3... c5 { Also playable. Your c pawn supports the extra pawn on d4. } 4. Nf3 { He develops before recovering d4, but your break already cleared the bishop's road. [%cal Bg1f3] }) (3... dxc3 { Also sound. You accept the pawn, but it opens lines for him too. } 4. Nxc3 { You strike a different bargain: extra material against his quicker development. [%cal Bb1c3] }) (3... Qe7 { Also playable. Your queen goes to e7. } 4. cxd4 4... Qxe4+ 5. Ne2 { Playable, and you grab a pawn with check, but your d5 break already freed the bishop without the detour. [%cal Bg1e2] }) (3... Ne7 { Also playable. Your knight goes to e7. } 4. Nf3 { He brings a piece out before collecting d4; your break already cleared the bishop's road. [%cal Bg1f3] }) (3... Nf6 { A sound developing move, but the center can chase your knight. } 4. e5 4... Nd5 5. Qxd4 { He develops the queen while collecting d4. } 5... Nb6 { Your knight has spent several moves getting here. The pawn break freed your other pieces for nothing. [%cal Bd5b6] }) 4. exd5 { He trades the pawn attacking e4, not the one on d4. Recapture with your queen. [%cal Yd8d5] } 4... Qxd5 { Your queen recaptures, and the diagonal is finally clear for the bishop. [%tail] [%cal Gd8d5] } (4... dxc3 { Also playable. You exchange another pawn before developing. } 5. Nxc3 { This stays playable, but recapturing on d5 already opened the bishop's road. [%cal Bb1c3] }) (4... Bd6 { Also playable. Your bishop goes to d6. } 5. Nf3 { He develops before recovering d4; recapturing on d5 already had your bishop's road open. [%cal Bg1f3] }) (4... Be7 { Also playable. Your bishop goes to e7. } 5. Nf3 { He brings a piece out before collecting d4, but your queen recapture already opened that road. [%cal Bg1f3] }) (4... Nf6 { Also sound. You develop before recovering the d pawn. } 5. Bb5+ { He develops with check before collecting d4. } 5... Nbd7 6. Qxd4 { The queen takes d4 — a pawn could have too, but recapturing on d5 already won the pawn back for you. [%cal Bd1d4] }) 5. cxd4 { He restores the material, and now it is time to collect on the bishop's new diagonal. } 5... Nc6 { Your knight adds pressure on d4 and clears the way further. [%cal Gb8c6] } 6. Nf3 { He brings his last knight out to guard the center. } 6... Bg4 { Your bishop is finally out, pinning the knight to the queen behind it — the diagonal you opened three moves ago. [%cal Gc8g4] } 0-1


