{ Now let us fix and restrict a weak pawn: a backward pawn cannot advance safely, and no other pawn can defend it. Push to e5 so his stays stuck forever. [%cal Ye4e5] } 1. e5 { The d6 pawn cannot escape to d5. Your pawn joins the attack without trading a rook for it. [%tail] [%cal Ge4e5] } (1. Rxd6 { That spends a rook on a pawn before adding the extra attacker. } 1... Bxd6 2. Bxd6 2... Rxd6 3. Qd5 3... Rxd5 4. cxd5 { The exchanges leave you materially behind. Add the pawn attack before taking on d6. [%cal Rc4d5] }) 1... Qc6 { His queen sidesteps, but the backward pawn still cannot move. } 2. h3 { You make luft and keep improving while he searches for a plan. [%cal Gh2h3] } 2... Kf8 { His king shuffles; the d6 pawn is still stuck fast. } 3. Bg3 { Your bishop adds itself to the pile on d6. [%cal Gf4g3] } 3... Qe4 { His queen jumps into your position, but it does not save the pawn. } 4. exd6 { The backward pawn finally falls, yours for nothing in return. [%cal Ge5d6] } 1-0


